<h1>Webhook endpoints</h1>

<p>Domain events delivered over HTTP. A pattern ending in a dot matches a whole
domain ("rental."); anything else is one exact event name.</p>

<%%= link_to "New endpoint", new_admin_webhook_endpoint_path %>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Event patterns</th>
      <th>URL</th>
      <th>Active</th>
      <th>Status</th>
      <th></th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <%% @records.each do |record| %>
      <tr>
        <td><%%= record.patterns.join(", ") %></td>
        <td><%%= record.url %></td>
        <td><%%= record.active? ? "yes" : "no" %></td>
        <td><%%= record.active? ? "active" : "disabled (#{record.disabled_reason})" %></td>
        <td><%%= button_to "Delete", admin_webhook_endpoint_path(record), method: :delete, form: { style: "display:inline" } %></td>
      </tr>
    <%% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>

<p>Each delivery is signed twice: <code>X-OpenLoam-Signature: sha256=HMAC-SHA256(secret, body)</code> (kept for
existing receivers) and <code>X-OpenLoam-Signature-V2: t=&lt;unix&gt;,v1=HMAC-SHA256(secret, "&lt;t&gt;.&lt;body&gt;")</code>,
which new receivers should verify. Read the secret with <code>OpenLoam::WebhookEndpoint#secret</code> in a console;
it is not shown here.</p>
